Description: Accept an already configured loopback in a fresh network namespace
 gVisor creates the loopback address before bubblewrap configures it. Request
 the same address idempotently; retain the namespace, address, ACK and link-up
 operations, including every error check. No network interface is shared.
Bug: https://github.com/google/gvisor/issues/13438
Bug: https://github.com/containers/bubblewrap/issues/745
--- a/network.c
+++ b/network.c
@@ -159,8 +159,11 @@ loopback_setup (void)
   if (r < 0)
     die_with_error ("loopback: Failed to bind NETLINK_ROUTE socket");
 
+  /* Some kernels configure lo when creating the network namespace. Adding
+   * the same address must be idempotent; all other setup failures are fatal.
+   * This does not change the namespace or introduce an external interface. */
   header = rtnl_setup_request (buffer, RTM_NEWADDR,
-                               NLM_F_CREATE | NLM_F_EXCL | NLM_F_ACK,
+                               NLM_F_CREATE | NLM_F_ACK,
                                sizeof (struct ifaddrmsg));
   addmsg = NLMSG_DATA (header);
 
